# Extra Python dependencies for the packaged app (mac + win bundles).
#
# Why this file exists: the bundle's requirements.txt is compiled ONLY from the
# root pyproject.toml, which does not depend on the internal packages under
# colrev/packages/*/. Those packages declare their own third-party deps in their
# own pyproject.toml, so those deps never reach the bundle (which installs with
# --no-deps). List here the top-level distributions the app actually needs; uv
# resolves their transitive deps automatically.
#
# Workflow when the app raises `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'X'`:
#   1. Map X to its PyPI distribution (e.g. bs4 -> beautifulsoup4).
#   2. Add the distribution name as one line below.
#   3. Regenerate + commit requirements.txt (see scripts/BUNDLE_DEPS.md).
#   4. Rebuild.
#
# Keep this minimal — only add what the app uses, to avoid bloating the bundle.

pyalex
beautifulsoup4
